<title>FRANCE: France sells 22.8 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 22.8 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury sold the following government bonds (BTANs) at auction on Thursday.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.APR.99	4.75	  9.630 BLN	   3.49</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 23.150 BLN/2.4		   NIL		102.59</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 20.0						    05.FEB</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.OCT.01	5.50	 13.170 BLN	  4.45</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 19.250 BLN/1.5		  100 MLN	   104.29</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 80.0						    12.FEB</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT OFFER</p>
<p>							     N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 21 to 23 billion francs of BTANs in total today. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 1.8.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
